  "definitions": {
    "hash": "SLotH reported active engine clocks; project actual Keccak round updates or SHA256 rounds plus feed-forward.",
    "transfer": "Hash-exclusive hash-MMIO occupancy. All three project variants have no such interface and contribute zero in this category.",
    "remaining": "Total minus Hash minus Transfer, including non-overlapped formatting, internal movement and instruction/controller work."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Single matched 33-byte first KAT per backend; actual full signature and signature cache checked against the KAT.",
    "SLotH Hash includes in-engine load, PRF setup and chain padding; corresponding project formatting outside the primitive is Remaining.",
    "An internal handoff can overlap Hash; it is diagnostic and is not added again as Transfer.",
    "P1U1 is the project comparison configuration, not a claim of identical microarchitecture to SLotH.",
    "All bars use measured cycles, a common zero baseline, and the same linear y scale; no frequency conversion or extrapolation."
  ],
